Instead of updating TypeORM why not use the built-in feature for making your entity type-safe.  Implementing this you don't have to sacrifice your TypeScript implementation against your project and/or implement the bang("!") on the class definition.

A bit new to TypeORM so maybe not as clean as I am assuming here but I think this helps bypass the default value of your entity instead of dropping it in a class, as the class would look for the constructor or default value.  And a default value on the entity is considered a bad practice due to the danger it proposes. 

