On a column with a simple check contraint, modification aren't detected during the migration generate.

### Expected Behavior

 ```typescript
@Column({ name: 'test', type: 'text', enum: ['TEST1','TEST2','TEST3'] })
 @Check('test_type_chk', "test IN ('TEST1','TEST2','TEST3')")
  test: TestType;
```

When we change the check constraint in the entity, it should be changed in the generated migration too.

### Actual Behavior

 ```typescript
@Column({ name: 'test', type: 'text', enum: ['TEST1','TEST2','TEST3'] })
 @Check('test_type_chk', "test IN ('TEST1','TEST2','TEST3')")
  test: TestType;
```

In a situation like above, when we modify the check in the entity, it's not updated in the generated migration.

### Steps to reproduce

On a simple table with a check constraint, change the constraint and generate a migration to see if it was ignored.

### My Environment

Nest: 9.2.1,
TypeOrm: 0.3.20

