To propose a solution we could maybe do the following:

- The single-JoinColumn path divergence was introduced in [#10672](https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/pull/10672) (composite key fix) — it switched from `getEntityValueMap()` → `createValueMap()` (which has bigint `String()` protection from [#720](https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/issues/720)) to `getEntityValue()` (which doesn't). Restoring consistency here is a minimal fix. (see #12407)
- For aurora-postgres specifically: upstream `typeorm-aurora-data-api-driver` needs `longReturnType: "STRING"` — tracked in [typeorm-aurora-data-api-driver#121](https://github.com/ArsenyYankovsky/typeorm-aurora-data-api-driver/issues/121).
- Longer-term, if drivers move to separate packages, each driver owns the contract of returning bigints as strings — core shouldn't need these safety nets.



