FK not getting updated after lazy loaded relation is loaded unless relation is set to undefined first

### Expected Behavior

```
export class TaskEntity {
    @Column({
	nullable: false
    })
    userId: number;

    @ManyToOne(() => UserEntity, user => user.tasks)
    user: Promise<user>;
}
```

if we have loaded a user's tasks
```
const user1 = await this.getUserById(1);
const user2 = await this.getUserById(1);
const tasks = await user1.tasks;
```
and after that we try to update the user relation of a task

```
task.userId = user2.id;
await this.dataSource.save(task);
```

the FK should get updated



### Actual Behavior

the FK doesn't get updated
if we try 👇
```
task.user = Promise.resolve(user2);
task.userId = user2.id;
await this.dataSource.save(task);
```
we get error from DB that Column 'userId' cannot be null
the only thing that works is to set the task's user to undefined first
set the userId to the new value
and save
```
task.user = undefined;
task.userId = user2.id;
await this.dataSource.save(task);
```
this is a wierd behavior
I spent a lot of time trouble shooting today
I absolutely love typeorm, and it's easy to use practical features
but the lazy loaded relations have odd behaviors sometimes

thanks. best of luck

